## THE FULL ENCLOSING FUNCTION — inlined because four readers once wrote the same broken line into a function none of them had read the tail of

`arm_coproc_i80321_6()` runs `:304-418`. Structure, complete:

```c
void arm_coproc_i80321_6(struct cpu *cpu, int opcode1, int opcode2, int l_bit,
	int crn, int crm, int rd)
{
	switch (crm) {
	case 0:	switch (crn) {
		case 0:	/* inten  -- THE ARM UNDER TEST (read died; write always silent) */
		case 4:	/* isteer -- read SILENT; write non-zero -> fatal+exit(1) at :320-322 */
		case 8:	/* isrc   -- read SILENT; write -> fatal+exit(1) at :330-331 */
		default:goto unknown;
		}
		break;
	case 1:	/* timers: tmr0 tmr1 tcr0 tcr1 trr0 trr1 tisr wdtcr -- 16 quiet arms.
		   tcr0/tcr1 READS INCREMENT the counter ("Ugly hack"); tisr write is
		   write-1-to-clear and calls INTERRUPT_DEASSERT. */
		default:goto unknown;
		}
		break;
	default:goto unknown;
	}

	return;                                    /* <-- the common tail */

unknown:
	fatal("arm_coproc_i80321_6: unimplemented opcode1=%i opcode2=%i crn="
	    "%i crm=%i rd=%i l=%i)\n", opcode1, opcode2, crn, crm, rd, l_bit);
	exit(1);
}
```

**Note `opcode1` and `opcode2` are NEVER TESTED for dispatch** — they appear only in that final
diagnostic's argument list. Every MRC/MCR to a given (crm, crn) reaches the same arm whatever the
opcodes are.

## SETTLED — do not re-derive, but DO challenge

* **The fix is member 4 ACCEPT of the option set**, on the footbridge IRQEnable precedent: the model
  ALREADY computes the right value (`r[rd] = i80321_inten`) and then discards it via `exit(1)`. There
  is no event to announce, so no latch and no bounded announce. **A `(once)` diagnostic here would
  ship a wrong record in product code** — printing "unimplemented" about a read that is implemented.
* **The write path was ALWAYS silent**, before and after. Only READS died. The fix makes crn 0's read
  behave exactly like its two siblings crn 4 and crn 8, whose reads are already silent-accept. **The
  arm under review was the file's own outlier**, and the fix removes the outlier rather than adding a
  policy.
* **`i80321_inten` is functionally wired, not dead storage** — the interrupt controller reads it via
  `d->enable`, and the probe's ANCHOR rows show an IRQ reaching vector `0x18` only when bit 28 is set.
* **Test-first is satisfied by one script in two colours**: `witness_committed.out` SCORE **11/26**,
  `witness_fix.out` SCORE **26/26**. Rung 3, cold debugger, unmodified in-tree machine, no
  `device_add`.

